If you're wondering why both and not just GPL-3.0
──────────────────────────────────────────────────
GPL-3.0 is the preferred license here — it is strong copyleft, well understood
in the free software world, and ensures that modifications to this packaging
code cannot be folded into a closed product without sharing them back.

However, this channel packages and distributes the Brave Origin binary, and
Brave is licensed under MPL-2.0 by Brave Software, Inc. As a distributor of
that binary, it is reasonable to honour the spirit of Brave's own license by
making the packaging code available under MPL-2.0 as well. This keeps the
licensing of the wrapper consistent with the software it wraps.

MPL-2.0 is also a copyleft license, but a weaker one — it only requires
modifications to MPL-licensed files to be shared, not the larger work around
them. That is why GPL-3.0 is the stronger and preferred choice for this project.

In short: GPL-3.0 is what this project stands behind. MPL-2.0 is offered
alongside it out of respect for Brave's license, given that this channel exists
specifically to distribute Brave Origin.

If you just want to use the channel, none of this matters — do whatever you want.
If you are redistributing or building on top of it, GPL-3.0 is recommended.
